  "forum.post6.title": { "pt-BR": "Impactos do descarte inadequado de plástico em ecossistemas de mangue", "en-US": "Impacts of improper plastic disposal on mangrove ecosystems", es: "Impacts of improper plastic disposal on mangrove ecosystems", fr: "Impacts of improper plastic disposal on mangrove ecosystems", de: "Impacts of improper plastic disposal on mangrove ecosystems", it: "Impacts of improper plastic disposal on mangrove ecosystems" },
  "forum.post6.content": { "pt-BR": "Pesquisando para a disciplina de Ecologia Marinha encontrei dados alarmantes: estima-se que 80% do plástico nos oceanos vem de rios, e os manguezais funcionam como \"filtros\" retendo grande parte desse material. Mas essa acumulação causa sérios danos à biota local. Compartilhando alguns dados para quem estiver estudando o tema.", "en-US": "Researching for the Marine Ecology course I found alarming data: an estimated 80% of plastic in the oceans comes from rivers, and mangroves act as \"filters\" retaining much of this material. But this accumulation causes serious damage to the local biota. Sharing some data for those studying the topic.", es: "Researching for the Marine Ecology course I found alarming data: an estimated 80% of plastic in the oceans comes from rivers, and mangroves act as \"filters\" retaining much of this material. But this accumulation causes serious damage to the local biota. Sharing some data for those studying the topic.", fr: "Researching for the Marine Ecology course I found alarming data: an estimated 80% of plastic in the oceans comes from rivers, and mangroves act as \"filters\" retaining much of this material. But this accumulation causes serious damage to the local biota. Sharing some data for those studying the topic.", de: "Researching for the Marine Ecology course I found alarming data: an estimated 80% of plastic in the oceans comes from rivers, and mangroves act as \"filters\" retaining much of this material. But this accumulation causes serious damage to the local biota. Sharing some data for those studying the topic.", it: "Researching for the Marine Ecology course I found alarming data: an estimated 80% of plastic in the oceans comes from rivers, and mangroves act as \"filters\" retaining much of this material. But this accumulation causes serious damage to the local biota. Sharing some data for those studying the topic." },
